  "rationale": "The final studio album by the Clifford Brown-Max Roach Quintet, and the first to feature Sonny Rollins on tenor sax (replacing Harold Land). A defining statement of the quintet's mature hard-bop language: Rollins brings a sharper, more angular edge to the front line, and the interplay between Brown's burnished trumpet and Rollins' thematic invention produces some of the finest ensemble jazz of the 1950s. Consensus across Penguin Guide, AllMusic, DownBeat, and The Rolling Stone Jazz Record Guide. Also notable as the last studio recordings by Brown and pianist Richie Powell before their deaths in June 1956 \u2014 the album carries an elegiac weight in the canon.",
